      "passageId": "wikipedia://Loose_(Nelly_Furtado_album)#p1",
      "snippet": "Loose is the third studio album by Canadian singer and songwriter Nelly Furtado, released on 6 June 2006 by Geffen Records and the Mosley Music Group. Following the release of Furtado's second album, Folklore (2003) through DreamWorks Records, it was announced that Universal Music Group would acquire DreamWorks Records, the later was folded into the Interscope Geffen A & M umbrella where Furtado would release any new music. Timbaland and his protégé Danja produced the bulk of the album, which incorporates influences of dance, R & B and hip hop. The album explores the theme of female sexuality and has been described as introspective or even sad in parts.",
